Third-party software in gooey-3d release archives
=================================================

gooey-3d itself is MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE). Most of
this file is about `gooey-cad-worker`, the separate executable that
`gooey-3d cad` runs. It is a Bun single-file executable built from
`cad-worker/` in this repository. Release archives append the full licence
texts of the npm packages below, copied from the exact versions in
cad-worker/bun.lock.


gooey-cad-worker
----------------

Sources, lockfile and build script:
  https://github.com/gooey-audio/3d/tree/main/cad-worker
  (cad-worker/package.json pins exact versions; cad-worker/bun.lock; cad-worker/build.sh)

Rebuild it with `cad-worker/build.sh` (needs bun). The OpenCascade WebAssembly
module is embedded as a separate asset and loaded at run time from its bytes
(cad-worker/src/wasm-bun.ts, runtime.ts). To use a modified build of the
library, replace the `replicad-opencascadejs` dependency (or its .wasm file)
and run build.sh again. You can also run the worker from source under Node
with GOOEY_CAD_WORKER="node cad-worker/src/worker.ts".

* OpenCascade Technology, as compiled to WebAssembly by replicad-opencascadejs 1.2.1
  Licence: GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 (LGPL-2.1-only), with the
  Open CASCADE exception
  https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT
  https://github.com/sgenoud/replicad (packages/replicad-opencascadejs)
  The WASM module and its Emscripten JavaScript glue are distributed unmodified.

* Bun runtime (embedded by `bun build --compile`), bun 1.3.x
  Licence: MIT. Bun statically links JavaScriptCore and other WebKit code,
  which are LGPL-2.0 (Bun's modified WebKit sources are at
  https://github.com/oven-sh/WebKit), and several other libraries under
  permissive licences.
  Bun's full third-party list: https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/main/LICENSE.md

* replicad 1.2.1, MIT. https://github.com/sgenoud/replicad
  - opentype.js 2.0.0, MIT. https://github.com/opentypejs/opentype.js
  - flatbush 4.7.0, ISC. https://github.com/mourner/flatbush
  - flatqueue 3.1.0, ISC. https://github.com/mourner/flatqueue

* manifold-3d 3.5.5 (Manifold compiled to WebAssembly), Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/elalish/manifold

Not shipped: manifold-3d's npm package brings its own CLI dependencies
(sharp, esbuild-wasm, gltf-transform) into node_modules. The worker does not
import them, so they are not in the executable.


gooey-3d
--------

gooey-3d statically links Rust crates (see Cargo.lock) and Manifold
(Apache-2.0) through manifold-csg. Their licences are permissive (MIT,
Apache-2.0, BSD, Zlib, Unicode); each crate's licence is in its published
package.
